WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.168
-Our next guest
is the lead singer

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:04.637
of the iconic rock band The Who.

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:06.706
He can be seen
in the new documentary

00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:08.440
"Rock Camp: The Movie,"

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:10.977
which is available now on
all major streaming platforms.

00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:13.812
Please welcome Roger Daltrey!

00:00:13.812 --> 00:00:17.250
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yes, my man! Come on!

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.585
That's my man!
-Hey, Jimmy.

00:00:19.585 --> 00:00:22.688
-Roger, welcome back
to the show.

00:00:22.688 --> 00:00:25.558
You know, I love having you
on the show.

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:26.960
We've been very lucky
to have you on.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:27.860
Thank you so much.

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:29.462
The last time you guys came on,

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:30.797
we did
a "Classroom Instruments."

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:32.532
And we did
"Won't Get Fooled Again."

00:00:32.532 --> 00:00:34.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:35.935
-Oh, dear.

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:38.270
Jim, now, I've got to tell you,
the Roots,

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:40.939
they're one of my favorite bands
of all time.

00:00:40.939 --> 00:00:43.209
[ Cheers and applause ]
They're fantastic musicians.

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:45.744
-We've been called --
-I got to say,

00:00:45.744 --> 00:00:48.815
I've never had so much fun
singing that song

00:00:48.815 --> 00:00:51.284
other than the first time
I sang it on the record.

00:00:51.284 --> 00:00:52.885
That was fun.
-Wow.

00:00:52.885 --> 00:00:56.055
-But doing it with the Roots
on those instruments,

00:00:56.055 --> 00:00:57.924
that was so refreshing.

00:00:57.924 --> 00:00:59.792
It brought it back to life.

00:00:59.792 --> 00:01:01.660
It was fabulous.

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:03.896
I absolutely loved it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:03.896 --> 00:01:06.365
And thank you, guys.
You were fabulous.

00:01:06.365 --> 00:01:07.733
-We've been called --

00:01:07.733 --> 00:01:09.802
Tariq calls us
the Dream Team of late night.

00:01:09.802 --> 00:01:11.337
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.337 --> 00:01:12.705
I'll let him have that,
but we are.

00:01:12.705 --> 00:01:15.808
But obviously, The Who
is an iconic rock band,

00:01:15.808 --> 00:01:18.845
but you as a lead singer
of the band,

00:01:18.845 --> 00:01:22.982
not only your singing
but your fashion,

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:26.219
but also your -- the swinging of
the microphone.

00:01:26.219 --> 00:01:29.288
That is iconic, and no one else
can do it without me going,

00:01:29.288 --> 00:01:30.923
"That's Roger Daltrey."

00:01:30.923 --> 00:01:33.425
When did you do it first
and go like,

00:01:33.425 --> 00:01:35.829
"Well, that could be my thing"?

00:01:35.829 --> 00:01:38.731
-I did it out of pure boredom,
actually,

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:43.002
because I was on a stage
with two maniacs

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:45.471
and a very straight bass player.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.471 --> 00:01:47.106
And I just got bored
and I thought,

00:01:47.106 --> 00:01:49.408
"I've got this thing in my hand
that I'm fed up

00:01:49.408 --> 00:01:51.176
with holding up there.

00:01:51.176 --> 00:01:52.412
What do I do with it?"

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:57.016
So I kind of threw it
and held on to the cord.

00:01:57.016 --> 00:01:59.185
And, of course, it came back,

00:01:59.185 --> 00:02:01.053
and I thought,
"Well, that was interesting.

00:02:01.053 --> 00:02:03.523
Let's see what more
I could do with it."

00:02:03.523 --> 00:02:07.293
And I went on to be quite good
with that thing.

00:02:07.293 --> 00:02:09.995
I mean, I could take a cigarette
out of someone's mouth

00:02:09.995 --> 00:02:14.534
from about 20 yards,
which is quite good, you know?

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:16.235
-Oh, my gosh. That's crazy.

00:02:16.235 --> 00:02:19.105
-Yeah, I was a really, really
good shot with that thing.

00:02:19.105 --> 00:02:20.907
But I can't see it now,
of course.

00:02:20.907 --> 00:02:22.375
-Yeah, well, no.

00:02:22.375 --> 00:02:24.643
-I throw it up in the air,
and I just pray

00:02:24.643 --> 00:02:28.648
that it comes down somewhere
within that kind of --

00:02:28.648 --> 00:02:31.350
-So it can hear
your voice somewhere. Yeah.

00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:33.252
Is there an earthquake
where you are, Roger?

00:02:33.252 --> 00:02:34.353
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.353 --> 00:02:36.789
-No, we don't have earthquakes.

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:38.691
Oh, it's my foot on the camera.

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:41.527
[ Laughter ]
-Stop doing that!

00:02:41.527 --> 00:02:42.828
Don't do that!
It's not your thing!

00:02:42.828 --> 00:02:45.431
-Oh, no, no!
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:47.366
-No, I don't want that
to be your thing.

00:02:47.366 --> 00:02:49.034
-It's Moon come back
to haunt us!

00:02:49.034 --> 00:02:51.904
He's in the next room!
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.904 --> 00:02:53.973
-Do you remember --
You obviously remember

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:56.275
"The Smothers Brothers"
when you guys went on to

00:02:56.275 --> 00:02:58.778
"The Smothers Brothers" --
he put, like, explosives

00:02:58.778 --> 00:03:02.415
in his drum and blew up
the drum set live

00:03:02.415 --> 00:03:04.650
and didn't tell anyone
on TV.

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:08.922
-No, that was -- it was planned
for a little bit of smoke

00:03:08.922 --> 00:03:12.258
and the skin was going to break.

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:16.629
But Moon being Moon decided
this wasn't grand enough.

00:03:16.629 --> 00:03:20.666
And I think he got
the pyrotechnic man drunk

00:03:20.666 --> 00:03:25.738
with a bottle of brandy
and talked him into putting

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:28.641
about 10 times the amount
of powder in the cannon

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:30.276
that was supposed to be there.

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:33.178
And it was literally like
a hand grenade going off.

00:03:33.178 --> 00:03:35.581
If you look at the film
and you study the film a bit --

00:03:35.581 --> 00:03:39.018
you can see it on YouTube --

00:03:39.018 --> 00:03:42.688
you see Pete banging his head.

00:03:42.688 --> 00:03:45.758
And Pete is about 10 feet
from the drum kit.

00:03:45.758 --> 00:03:47.693
And he's patting his head
like this.

00:03:47.693 --> 00:03:49.762
And what he's trying to do
is put his hair out.

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:52.197
His hair is on fire.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.197 --> 00:03:54.734
-We have that clip.
I want to show everyone.

00:03:54.734 --> 00:03:56.435
Here's The Who
from "The Smothers Brothers."

00:03:56.435 --> 00:03:58.004
Check this out.

00:04:05.445 --> 00:04:08.381
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.381 --> 00:04:12.518
Oh, my God! Oh, my God!

00:04:12.518 --> 00:04:16.088
[ Laughter ]
Yo!

00:04:16.088 --> 00:04:17.523
Yo!

00:04:17.523 --> 00:04:20.092
That's the greatest clip ever.

00:04:20.092 --> 00:04:22.795
Yeah. I don't know how --
I just love you guys.

00:04:22.795 --> 00:04:25.231
I want to talk about
"Rock Camp: The Movie"

00:04:25.231 --> 00:04:27.165
because I loved it,

00:04:27.165 --> 00:04:30.736
and obviously, you know
I'm a fan of rock 'n' roll.

00:04:30.736 --> 00:04:34.073
And I think everyone,
in the back of their minds,

00:04:34.073 --> 00:04:35.441
wants to be a rock star.

00:04:35.441 --> 00:04:39.111
You know, and I think
this rock 'n' roll fantasy camp,

00:04:39.111 --> 00:04:40.946
you go like,
"Wow, that's interesting.

00:04:40.946 --> 00:04:44.450
I get to jam out
and meet these icons."

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:49.688
And you just get to
sing with Roger Daltrey.

00:04:49.688 --> 00:04:52.825
What made you say yes for
the first time in doing this?

00:04:52.825 --> 00:04:58.330
-I said yes mainly, well, first
of all, I got invited to do it

00:04:58.330 --> 00:05:01.567
for a charity thing for Levon
Helm, the drummer of The Band.

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:03.936
-Yeah, absolutely.
-And I was a huge fan of Levon,

00:05:03.936 --> 00:05:06.172
and I just wanted to meet him
and tell him --

00:05:06.172 --> 00:05:08.407
'cause he just got over
throat cancer.

00:05:08.407 --> 00:05:11.344
And they were doing a fundraiser
for him.

00:05:11.344 --> 00:05:14.546
So I decided to go along
and have a look.

00:05:14.546 --> 00:05:18.384
What it did for me was remind me
of all the reasons

00:05:18.384 --> 00:05:20.052
why I did this
in the first place.

00:05:20.052 --> 00:05:23.989
I did it because we were young
and we were having so much fun.

00:05:23.989 --> 00:05:26.992
And we were just fans of music.

00:05:26.992 --> 00:05:31.364
Simple, very simple living
and playing music.

00:05:31.364 --> 00:05:34.266
We'd do anything
just to play music.

00:05:34.266 --> 00:05:38.904
And I was with people of
varying abilities of playing,

00:05:38.904 --> 00:05:41.240
some very good, incidentally.

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:43.009
Some of them extremely good,

00:05:43.009 --> 00:05:45.978
but some of them [Laughs]
extremely bad.

00:05:45.978 --> 00:05:49.314
-Yeah, of course.
-And it makes it fun.

00:05:49.314 --> 00:05:53.252
It's good to be reminded of
where you started.

00:05:53.252 --> 00:05:55.254
'Cause we've been around
so long now,

00:05:55.254 --> 00:05:57.023
I feel like we're the wallpaper.

00:05:57.023 --> 00:06:00.359
I mean --
-No. No.

00:06:00.359 --> 00:06:04.163
-And it's just good to be
reminded that, when we started,

00:06:04.163 --> 00:06:09.235
how simple, and how -- we were
just doing it for the music.

00:06:09.235 --> 00:06:12.538
We didn't know how far it would
take us, and look where we are.

00:06:12.538 --> 00:06:13.772
-Yeah.
-It's wonderful.

00:06:13.772 --> 00:06:16.208
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:16.208 --> 00:06:18.678
You'll never be the wallpaper.

00:06:18.678 --> 00:06:21.714
Yeah, that's my man!
Roger Daltrey, the one and only!

00:06:21.714 --> 00:06:24.050
"Rock Camp: The Movie"
is out now.

